#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# factorial_power

#% text
# `factorial_power(x, n)` gives the falling factorial x (x - 1) ... (x - n + 1).

#% text
# `factorial_power(x, n, h)` gives x (x - h) ... (x - (n - 1) h).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integer n give the product; numbers otherwise gamma(x + 1)/gamma(x - n + 1).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
factorial_power(x, 3)
#% output
#= x*(-2 + x)*(-1 + x)

#% cell
factorial_power(10, 3)
#% output
#= 720

#% cell
factorial_power(x, 3, 2)
#% output
#= x*(-4 + x)*(-2 + x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `pochhammer`, `factorial`, `binomial`
